{"availability":"available","full":"nedonatelli/sidecar","name":"sidecar","description":"Free, self-hosted AI coding assistant for VS Code — local Ollama models, Anthropic Claude, or any OpenAI-compatible server. Full agent loop with tool use, inline completions, and MCP support.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":8,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-03T20:01:23Z","updated":"2026-10-07T10:32:18Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nedonatelli.github.io/sidecar/","topics":["agent","ai-coding-assistant","anthropic","code-completion","copilot-alternative","local-llm","mcp","ollama","openai-compatible","tool-use","typescript","vscode-extension"],"demo":"https://nedonatelli.github.io/sidecar/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:19.618Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:19.618Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:19.618Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T11:15:19.618Z","stars":8,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SideCar is a free, self-hosted VS Code extension that serves as a drop-in replacement for GitHub Copilot and Claude Code. Use local Ollama models, the Anthropic API, OpenAI, Fireworks AI, OpenRouter, Google Gemini, Groq, AWS Bedrock, your GitHub Copilot subscription, Kickstand (self-hosted), or any OpenAI-compatible server (vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp, a gateway) for AI-powered coding — with full agentic capabilities, inline completions, and tool use.","A free, open-source, local-first autonomous AI agent for coding — a full agent loop, not just chat. No subscription, and with local models, no data leaves your machine.","Agent mode, tool use, and MCP are table stakes in 2026 — Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code, Cline, and Continue all have them. What sets SideCar apart is the combination underneath, all with no subscription:"],"features":["Genuinely free and fully local-first — runs offline on Ollama with no API key or required cloud; plug in a frontier provider only when you want one.","Tool-call recovery from model text — many capable local models emit their tool calls as plain text or JSON in the content field instead of the structured toolcalls field, so a stock harness sees no call and stalls.…","Capability-adaptive gates — completion, syntax, red-check, grounding, and citation gates plus tiered reprompt budgets aimed at making weaker local models usable. Whether the net effect is a lift is measured, not assumed.","Parallelism & write-isolation — shadow workspaces (ephemeral git worktree), audit mode (in-memory write buffer), fork & parallel solve (N attempts, pick the winner), and typed sub-agent facets.","First-party VS Code integration — Problems-panel security/diagnostics, Test Explorer agent runs, CodeLens actions, file decorations, inline completions, and inline chat."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nedonatelli/sidecar/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"76eb3f832b5e6c9abb1c9d6e8e4e98e19f9c99832054552218dcea734416d77e","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:19.753Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:19.753Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SideCar is a free, self-hosted VS Code extension that serves as a drop-in replacement for GitHub Copilot and Claude Code. Use local Ollama models, the Anthropic API, OpenAI, Fireworks AI, OpenRouter, Google Gemini, Groq, AWS Bedrock, your GitHub Copilot subscription, Kickstand (self-hosted), or any OpenAI-compatible server (vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp, a gateway) for AI-powered coding — with full agentic capabilities, inline completions, and tool use.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nedonatelli/sidecar/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"not_required","text":"Genuinely free and fully local-first — runs offline on Ollama with no API key or required cloud; plug in a frontier provider only when you want one.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nedonatelli/sidecar/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","statu